\section*{Counting-hierarchy upper bound for existential-universal real sentences}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 141; 2026-10-04), the asserted result is that existential real feasibility, and more generally existential--universal real sentences with circuit-given integer polynomials, lie in a fixed counting-hierarchy level.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 141; 2026-10-04), critical-point deformation turns quantified fibers into short algebraic witnesses. Modular evaluation accesses huge controlled polynomials without expansion, while residue--trace determinant formulas and compressed derivative-sign labels recover the needed root signs inside the counting hierarchy.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The result supplies the conclusion in this problem with its displayed hypotheses and quantifiers. The broader statements and applications in the manuscript are kept separate from the particular question above. The supporting result is manuscript 1 (family 141; 2026-10-04).

\subsection{Formal verification}
